\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>The Fed on Dec 9 and CPI on Dec 10: a half-point hike or a 10-year yield well above 5% leans toward the worry.</li><li>The Q4 report on Jan 14, 2027: the reserve build, the card charge-off rate against 3.2%, and the first full 2027 guide.</li><li>A close above $359.80 or below $324.25.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Results and current guidance are solid. The earlier guidance figures come from one secondary source, and call colour from recaps. The core capital ratio read 13.9% in the release and 14.0% in the 10-Q. Succession detail is press reporting from unnamed sources. Peer credit figures are from one read each. Share prices are Webull daily bars, adjusted for dividends.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://pulse2.com/jpmorgan-chase-q3-2026-results\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release copy</a> · <a href=\"https://www.money365.market/articles/jp-morgan-q3-2026-earnings-analysis\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Analysis with prior guidance</a> · <a href=\"https://www.webull.com/news/15741198075913216\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Call transcript</a> · <a href=\"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3007181/jpmorgan-q3-earnings-call-highlights-capital-deployment-and-ai-risks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Call recap</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000019617/000162828026069523/jpm-20260930.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10-Q</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000001961726000096/jpm-20260402.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2026 proxy</a> · <a href=\"https://www.bankingdive.com/news/jpmorgans-lake-exits-petno-rohrbaugh-named-co-presidents/823738/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Co-presidents (Banking Dive)</a> · <a href=\"https://www.wealthprofessional.ca/news/industry-news/jpmorgan-sets-a-two-to-three-year-clock-on-naming-dimons-successor/392862\" target=\"_blank\" r